{%- comment -%}
  Besjaar — compare-at sale display (2026-09-27)

  Shows a compare-at-price sale in exactly the same style as an automatic
  Shopify discount (snippets/besjaar-discount-badge.liquid): the same badge
  slot and colours, the sale price in sale red and the earlier price struck
  through. Cards call it only when no automatic discount applies, so an
  automatic discount always wins.

  Here the reduced price IS the product price (variant.price), and
  compare_at_price is the earlier normal price. That is also what Google
  Merchant Center receives as price / sale price, so shop and Google match.
  Nothing here says "applied at checkout", because nothing is.

  PARAMETERS
    product  (required) the product to evaluate
    variant  (optional) the variant whose prices are used; defaults to
             product.selected_or_first_available_variant
    layout   'badge' — badge text, e.g. "36% KORTING"
             'price' — sale price + original struck through, for a card price element

  Renders nothing when the product has no compare-at price above its price.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bcs_variant = variant
  unless bcs_variant
    assign bcs_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  endunless
  assign bcs_price = bcs_variant.price
  assign bcs_was = bcs_variant.compare_at_price | default: 0
  assign bcs_pct = 0
  if bcs_was > bcs_price and bcs_price > 0
    comment
      Integer cents, so this rounds DOWN: the badge never claims more than the
      real saving (€39,99 → €25,49 is 36.26%, shown as 36%).
    endcomment
    assign bcs_pct = bcs_was | minus: bcs_price | times: 100 | divided_by: bcs_was
  endif
-%}

{%- if bcs_pct > 0 -%}
  {%- case layout -%}
    {%- when 'price' -%}
      <span class="bj-price__now">{{ bcs_price | money }}</span>
      <s class="bj-price__was"><span class="besjaar-ui-visually-hidden">{{ 'besjaar_ui.product.regular_price' | t }} </span>{{ bcs_was | money }}</s>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}Same wording as the other sale badges in the shop ("15% KORTING"), in every language.{%- endcomment -%}
      {{- bcs_pct }}% KORTING
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
